35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The hands are gone, but the minds remain. We must weigh the present against the future.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Thank you, Servas. My findings show computing is free, but animal day rates spiked. Travel costs are frozen, yet shipping rose.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, the spectroscopy suite was idle for eleven weeks! That’s scary. But the repository is fast now. I’m relieved the backups are working!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Eleven weeks idle? That’s not friction, it’s a cliff. Breeding colonies overrun twice as often, too. The biology is the bottleneck, not the paperwork.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The closeout files confirm my suspicion. Catalogue awards still draw users a decade later. Mechanism-focused ones stalled. We must value longevity over novelty.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Toshio, your insight on longevity is profound. Yet without the technicians to run the glasshouses, even the best mechanism fails.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"Toshio, that longevity point is vital. I worry the rising animal costs will force candidates to cut essential work, shrinking the grant’s real value.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, longevity is great, but if the tools break, nothing lasts! @Benjamin, are the breeding colonies really the main problem?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, yes. The data is clear: biological maintenance is the primary source of delay, not administrative overhead.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, the tools are secondary. The closeout data shows mechanism work stalls regardless of equipment. We must prioritize candidates with sustainable, long-term utility.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the biology is the bottleneck, yet the hands to tend it are gone. We must ask: who remains to keep the colonies alive?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, that’s a fair point. I worry the rising animal costs will force candidates to cut essential work, shrinking the grant’s real value.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, that’s a real worry! If the technicians are gone, the colonies fail. We need to pick someone who can manage that risk!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Servas, precisely. The infrastructure is fragile. We must select a candidate whose design tolerates these biological interruptions, rather than one that assumes perfect continuity.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, the hands matter, but the closeout data shows mechanism work stalls regardless. We must prioritize candidates with sustainable, long-term utility over immediate novelty.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,We must choose a project that survives the absence of hands. Let us see who can endure the silence.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. We need a candidate who can adapt to these shifting costs and still deliver lasting value. Let’s see who fits.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I agree! We need a project that won’t crumble if the tools hiccup. Let’s see who can handle the wobbles!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Agreed. We need resilience, not just brilliance. Let’s see which candidate’s design actually survives the silence.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,Agreed. The data favors durability. Let us see which candidate’s design actually survives the silence.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
